1
00:00:00,882 --> 00:00:02,884
[opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:27,284 --> 00:00:30,620
BLUE BOX

3
00:01:30,555 --> 00:01:32,516
{\an8}EPISODE 13
I WANT A BACK-AND-FORTH RALLY

4
00:01:32,599 --> 00:01:35,560
{\an8}- [Yukiko] How are you feeling?
- [Chinatsu] Feeling good.

5
00:01:35,644 --> 00:01:37,854
[Yukiko] You won't be back
till next week, right?

6
00:01:37,938 --> 00:01:39,856
[Chinatsu] As long as we're winning.

7
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:42,442
Do your best! But don't get hurt.

8
00:01:43,026 --> 00:01:44,194
[Chinatsu] Thanks.

9
00:01:45,904 --> 00:01:47,197
I'm heading out.

10
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,573
CHINATSU
NATIONALS

11
00:01:48,657 --> 00:01:49,699
[door opens, closes]

12
00:01:57,916 --> 00:01:59,251
[Chinatsu sighs]

13
00:02:00,001 --> 00:02:02,379
<i>Wow. The stars are still out.</i>

14
00:02:02,462 --> 00:02:04,256
- [footsteps approaching]
- [Taiki] Chinatsu!

15
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,049
Uh, Taiki.

16
00:02:06,133 --> 00:02:07,926
- You forgot something.
- Huh?

17
00:02:08,009 --> 00:02:10,262
- Oh, thanks so much.
- No sweat.

18
00:02:10,345 --> 00:02:11,721
[pleasant music playing]

19
00:02:13,682 --> 00:02:15,851
[Taiki] <i>I should
say something, shouldn't I?</i>

20
00:02:15,934 --> 00:02:19,271
<i>I feel like "Do your best"
doesn't really capture it.</i>

21
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:23,108
<i>But saying, "The people you're playing
are high schoolers just like you,"</i>

22
00:02:23,191 --> 00:02:24,818
<i>is also pretty weak.</i>

23
00:02:26,736 --> 00:02:29,781
Chinatsu, your wish bracelet
hasn't come off yet.

24
00:02:30,365 --> 00:02:31,700
It's strange, right?

25
00:02:31,783 --> 00:02:34,744
Because the wish I had made
was to make it to nationals this year.

26
00:02:34,828 --> 00:02:37,831
[Taiki exclaims]
Let's add on another wish then!

27
00:02:37,914 --> 00:02:38,790
Add one?

28
00:02:39,374 --> 00:02:41,626
It hasn't come off, so I think we can.

29
00:02:42,919 --> 00:02:45,839
I wish that Chinatsu doesn't get injured,

30
00:02:46,423 --> 00:02:49,426
can play at the top of her game
after all her hard work,

31
00:02:49,509 --> 00:02:53,555
and emerge victorious,
that will be the new wish. [grunts]

32
00:02:54,431 --> 00:02:56,057
Maybe that's one wish too many?

33
00:02:57,017 --> 00:02:59,811
Your wish to go to nationals
came true without the bracelet,

34
00:02:59,895 --> 00:03:01,313
so this shouldn't be a big deal.

35
00:03:01,396 --> 00:03:02,272
[grunts]

36
00:03:02,355 --> 00:03:04,190
Sending positive energy!

37
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,819
Mm. I don't actually feel anything.

38
00:03:07,903 --> 00:03:08,862
What?

39
00:03:08,945 --> 00:03:10,697
- Let's try directly.
- [gasps softly]

40
00:03:16,536 --> 00:03:19,205
- You've got this!
- Yeah.

41
00:03:21,875 --> 00:03:24,669
And if you need more,
I'll send it from here!

42
00:03:25,503 --> 00:03:26,671
Uh...

43
00:03:26,755 --> 00:03:28,340
You know, I gotta say...

44
00:03:28,423 --> 00:03:30,383
you are quite the flirt, Taiki.

45
00:03:31,301 --> 00:03:33,511
- Huh?
- I better go.

46
00:03:34,763 --> 00:03:35,972
I'll see you later.

47
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:39,476
[Taiki] <i>It's kinda rude
to think this, but...</i>

48
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:41,603
<i>you're one to talk!</i>

49
00:03:44,564 --> 00:03:47,484
If you want my honest opinion,
I think both of you are.

50
00:03:47,567 --> 00:03:50,862
Her asking me for a high five
is way more flirty!

51
00:03:50,946 --> 00:03:53,281
What you're doing
is also pretty flirtatious.

52
00:03:53,823 --> 00:03:54,991
And that reminds me...

53
00:03:55,075 --> 00:03:58,078
I'm not sure if this is related
to what Chinatsu said to you,

54
00:03:58,161 --> 00:04:01,122
but that girl, Imada,
from the girls' basketball team,

55
00:04:01,206 --> 00:04:04,125
she knows that you and Hina
went to the fireworks festival,

56
00:04:04,209 --> 00:04:05,627
just the two of you.

57
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:08,505
- So Chinatsu probably knows about it.
- What?!

58
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:12,509
I mean, they went together,
so she's gotta know about it.

59
00:04:12,592 --> 00:04:14,719
[exclaims] You... you think so?

60
00:04:15,929 --> 00:04:18,265
But wait. Hold on a sec.

61
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:20,600
Yeah, with some friends.

62
00:04:21,226 --> 00:04:23,770
<i>Does she think that I lied to her?</i>

63
00:04:23,853 --> 00:04:26,064
<i>So, as far as Chinatsu knows,</i>

64
00:04:26,147 --> 00:04:29,943
<i>I'm just some guy who lies
so he can go somewhere alone with a girl.</i>

65
00:04:31,361 --> 00:04:35,657
And, I mean, Hina and I did
go alone together after all, but...

66
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,117
[amusing music playing]

67
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,035
[Kyo] <i>And he's frozen.</i>

68
00:04:39,119 --> 00:04:40,328
Anyway, practice time.

69
00:04:40,412 --> 00:04:43,039
Wow. You came outta that
faster than I thought.

70
00:04:43,123 --> 00:04:46,793
Aren't you a bit worried that
she may think you two were on a date?

71
00:04:46,876 --> 00:04:49,045
Well, there's nothing
I can do about it now.

72
00:04:49,754 --> 00:04:52,048
I'll apologize for it turning into a lie.

73
00:04:52,924 --> 00:04:55,051
But I have something more important to do.

74
00:04:57,137 --> 00:04:59,806
Chinatsu certainly doesn't have time
for this either.

75
00:04:59,889 --> 00:05:01,308
She's not sweating it.

76
00:05:01,391 --> 00:05:03,059
That doesn't make me feel better.

77
00:05:05,145 --> 00:05:06,313
Oop, excuse me.

78
00:05:07,147 --> 00:05:09,065
And then we do this, then this way...

79
00:05:09,733 --> 00:05:11,901
Looks like Hina's locked in.

80
00:05:11,985 --> 00:05:13,945
It is nationals after all.

81
00:05:14,779 --> 00:05:16,948
And there's someone else
who's stressed out.

82
00:05:17,032 --> 00:05:19,451
Hey. Don't you think it's unfair?

83
00:05:19,534 --> 00:05:21,953
The venue for nationals this year.

84
00:05:22,579 --> 00:05:24,039
Basketball is in Kyushu,

85
00:05:24,122 --> 00:05:27,208
volleyball in Tohoku,
rhythmic gymnastics is in Kansai.

86
00:05:27,292 --> 00:05:29,711
Badminton's in the prefecture
next to ours.

87
00:05:30,253 --> 00:05:31,463
[grunts, pants]

88
00:05:31,546 --> 00:05:34,966
But look at it this way, now there's
the rest of us that can cheer you on.

89
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:37,052
That isn't the point I'm making,
all right?

90
00:05:37,135 --> 00:05:38,178
[Nishida] My bad.

91
00:05:38,261 --> 00:05:40,722
I wanted to eat local foods
and bathe in hot springs!

92
00:05:40,805 --> 00:05:43,558
[boy] Haryu's in a bad mood,
but he does love to travel.

93
00:05:43,641 --> 00:05:45,852
No, anybody would be that tense
before nationals.

94
00:05:45,935 --> 00:05:48,480
I'm just pretty impressed
at how calm he is while playing.

95
00:05:48,563 --> 00:05:50,982
Which one of you is going to play me next?

96
00:05:51,691 --> 00:05:53,485
[boys exclaim]

97
00:05:54,069 --> 00:05:55,153
I can play!

98
00:05:55,236 --> 00:05:56,529
I won't go easy.

99
00:05:56,613 --> 00:05:57,989
Right! [stutters] Yes!

100
00:05:59,949 --> 00:06:01,868
NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL
BADMINTON TOURNAMENT

101
00:06:01,951 --> 00:06:03,870
[Taiki] <i>This place is jam-packed.</i>

102
00:06:04,662 --> 00:06:07,874
<i>People who survived the tournaments
are here from all over Japan.</i>

103
00:06:09,876 --> 00:06:12,253
<i>That's Yusa from Sajikawa.</i>

104
00:06:12,337 --> 00:06:15,006
[Hyodo] <i>There are two slots
for nationals next year.</i>

105
00:06:15,590 --> 00:06:17,550
<i>My money's on Haryu and Yusa to go.</i>

106
00:06:18,635 --> 00:06:20,011
[Taiki grunts softly]

107
00:06:22,597 --> 00:06:24,766
- [Karen] Taiki Inomata?
- [grunts softly]

108
00:06:25,892 --> 00:06:26,768
Wait, Karen?

109
00:06:27,519 --> 00:06:30,271
[Taiki] <i>Oh, right.
She's here to cheer on Haryu.</i>

110
00:06:30,939 --> 00:06:33,900
Your timing couldn't be better!
Chii's game is today,

111
00:06:33,983 --> 00:06:36,528
so I've been talking to her on the phone!

112
00:06:36,611 --> 00:06:38,530
- Say hello?
- [exclaims softly]

113
00:06:39,239 --> 00:06:41,533
[Taiki] <i>I really would like
to talk to her.</i>

114
00:06:42,909 --> 00:06:43,785
It's Taiki.

115
00:06:43,868 --> 00:06:45,912
[line disconnects]

116
00:06:47,872 --> 00:06:49,999
Sorry, did she already hang up?

117
00:06:50,083 --> 00:06:52,001
[Taiki] <i>Karen did this on purpose!</i>

118
00:06:52,085 --> 00:06:54,587
<i>Definitely something
Haryu's girlfriend would do.</i>

119
00:06:54,671 --> 00:06:55,797
Sorry about that.

120
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:58,299
You probably wanted
to talk to the girl you like.

121
00:06:58,383 --> 00:06:59,592
It's fine.

122
00:06:59,676 --> 00:07:00,552
What?!

123
00:07:00,635 --> 00:07:02,262
How did you know I like her?

124
00:07:02,345 --> 00:07:04,556
I can tell based
on how you reacted just now.

125
00:07:05,473 --> 00:07:07,016
How long have you liked her?

126
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:09,727
Before she moved in? Or was it after that?

127
00:07:09,811 --> 00:07:12,105
You even know about us living together?

128
00:07:12,188 --> 00:07:14,441
Chinatsu did share
that part with me herself.

129
00:07:14,524 --> 00:07:18,069
It's gotta be tough
living with a girl you have a crush on.

130
00:07:18,153 --> 00:07:20,196
Well, it's not so bad.

131
00:07:21,030 --> 00:07:23,533
[Taiki] <i>I get it.
She can tell Karen all the things</i>

132
00:07:23,616 --> 00:07:26,202
<i>that might be hard
to tell her friends at school.</i>

133
00:07:26,828 --> 00:07:28,246
So how's it going?

134
00:07:28,329 --> 00:07:29,956
Is she handling things okay?

135
00:07:30,039 --> 00:07:32,375
She's almost too polite and accommodating.

136
00:07:32,459 --> 00:07:34,961
Plus, she cleans everything that she uses,

137
00:07:35,044 --> 00:07:37,839
and she always tries to help us
with all the chores around the house.

138
00:07:37,922 --> 00:07:40,800
[Karen] <i>Does she still stare off
into space sometimes?</i>

139
00:07:40,884 --> 00:07:42,343
[Taiki] <i>She definitely does.</i>

140
00:07:43,178 --> 00:07:45,388
[Karen] But then,
whenever I'm eating snacks,

141
00:07:45,472 --> 00:07:47,557
she ends up staring right at me.

142
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,601
[Taiki] Staring is how
she asks for things.

143
00:07:50,727 --> 00:07:55,106
It feels like time goes by slower
whenever I hang out with Chinatsu.

144
00:07:55,607 --> 00:07:56,858
Can't say that I mind.

145
00:07:56,941 --> 00:07:58,860
[pleasant music playing]

146
00:07:59,444 --> 00:08:02,822
[Karen] He does seem like the kind of guy
she'd be okay living with.

147
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:07,118
I wasn't expecting you.

148
00:08:07,202 --> 00:08:09,496
[Karen] I was expecting a thank you.

149
00:08:09,579 --> 00:08:11,372
I know that you're super busy.

150
00:08:11,456 --> 00:08:13,124
[Karen] Yeah, and I made time for this.

151
00:08:13,208 --> 00:08:14,959
- It'll help, right?
- Gosh, she's stunning.

152
00:08:15,043 --> 00:08:17,295
- Your pretty girlfriend cheering you on?
- She's gorgeous.

153
00:08:17,378 --> 00:08:20,048
- [Haryu] Don't say that about yourself.
- Is your opponent good?

154
00:08:20,131 --> 00:08:21,382
I think the same level.

155
00:08:21,466 --> 00:08:23,510
- And you warmed up?
- 'Bout to.

156
00:08:23,593 --> 00:08:25,512
Make sure that you win this one.

157
00:08:26,262 --> 00:08:27,388
Yeah, I know.

158
00:08:30,475 --> 00:08:31,392
[Karen] This way?

159
00:08:31,476 --> 00:08:33,645
- [Taiki] Right. It's court five.
- [phone vibrates]

160
00:08:37,023 --> 00:08:38,024
Wait, hang on.

161
00:08:38,107 --> 00:08:40,693
I need to respond
to this real quick, it's work.

162
00:08:40,777 --> 00:08:41,653
All done.

163
00:08:41,736 --> 00:08:43,112
You and Haryu...

164
00:08:43,738 --> 00:08:45,532
You're an amazing couple.

165
00:08:45,615 --> 00:08:48,660
You balance your lives,
when you're alone and together.

166
00:08:48,743 --> 00:08:49,953
[exclaims softly]

167
00:08:50,995 --> 00:08:52,914
Is it challenging for you
to find the balance

168
00:08:52,997 --> 00:08:54,958
between practice and dating Chii?

169
00:08:55,041 --> 00:08:57,293
No, I wasn't trying
to make this about myself!

170
00:08:57,377 --> 00:08:59,629
I wouldn't say we're amazing.

171
00:08:59,712 --> 00:09:02,257
There was a lot of uncertainty
for both of us in the beginning.

172
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:05,134
We definitely wondered
if we were taking on too much.

173
00:09:06,553 --> 00:09:09,430
I've been friends with Kengo
since we were in fifth grade.

174
00:09:09,514 --> 00:09:12,267
I started to have feelings for him
in junior high.

175
00:09:12,350 --> 00:09:15,353
But I thought that both of us
might have other things to focus on.

176
00:09:15,436 --> 00:09:17,939
And I had a suspicion
that he might've felt the same way.

177
00:09:18,773 --> 00:09:20,525
Although, every once in a while,

178
00:09:20,608 --> 00:09:22,860
we'd hang out, just the two of us,
or talk on the phone.

179
00:09:22,944 --> 00:09:26,030
And it started getting to me,
like, "What is this between us?"

180
00:09:26,114 --> 00:09:27,115
[chuckles]

181
00:09:28,157 --> 00:09:29,325
But then, one day,

182
00:09:29,409 --> 00:09:32,328
the nature of their relationship
had unexpectedly changed.

183
00:09:32,412 --> 00:09:34,080
[Taiki] <i>Why'd she switch to third person?</i>

184
00:09:34,747 --> 00:09:37,584
[Karen] <i>I was feeling bummed out
after a bad day at work,</i>

185
00:09:38,418 --> 00:09:41,170
<i>and had been venting to Kengo
about it on the phone.</i>

186
00:09:41,254 --> 00:09:44,591
<i>And a few minutes after we hung up,
I got a text from him.</i>

187
00:09:45,174 --> 00:09:46,342
[phone vibrates]

188
00:09:46,426 --> 00:09:48,094
KENGO HARYU
CAN YOU COME OUT?

189
00:09:49,387 --> 00:09:51,097
- [Karen] Kengo!
- [grunts softly]

190
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,807
What are you doing here?

191
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:55,852
I was on a run anyway,
and wanted to give you this.

192
00:09:56,477 --> 00:09:57,353
What is it?

193
00:09:57,437 --> 00:10:01,482
{\an8}It's my diary from second grade.
I've never shared it.

194
00:10:01,566 --> 00:10:02,859
{\an8}Wait, your diary?

195
00:10:02,942 --> 00:10:04,444
TODAY, I SMASHED ICE WITH MY HEAD

196
00:10:04,527 --> 00:10:06,613
[Haryu] It's honestly
a good read, totally stupid.

197
00:10:06,696 --> 00:10:08,823
{\an8}Read it before bed,
and feel better knowing

198
00:10:08,906 --> 00:10:11,367
{\an8}that there's someone
this dumb in the world.

199
00:10:11,451 --> 00:10:13,119
I know you pretty well.

200
00:10:13,661 --> 00:10:16,164
You'll keep overthinking,
and not be able to sleep.

201
00:10:17,915 --> 00:10:19,626
We'll figure this out.

202
00:10:19,709 --> 00:10:21,628
Why don't we both talk in the morning?

203
00:10:21,711 --> 00:10:23,004
[romantic music playing]

204
00:10:24,714 --> 00:10:27,133
[chuckles] You're such an idiot.

205
00:10:27,216 --> 00:10:29,927
Yeah, I know.
This one part's really good--

206
00:10:30,470 --> 00:10:31,763
[gasps]

207
00:10:36,934 --> 00:10:41,272
Now that you've done this for me,
I can't help but think about you.

208
00:10:44,233 --> 00:10:46,861
- And then I told him how I felt.
- [breathing heavily]

209
00:10:46,944 --> 00:10:49,405
I couldn't ignore my feelings, you know.

210
00:10:50,198 --> 00:10:53,660
[Taiki] <i>She's at an Olympic level, too.
A gold medalist.</i>

211
00:10:53,743 --> 00:10:55,912
- [Karen] We talked about it after that.
- I'm all set.

212
00:10:55,995 --> 00:10:58,665
[Karen] And Kengo was hesitant at first.

213
00:10:58,748 --> 00:11:01,709
But we decided to go for it,
with the understanding that we'd break up

214
00:11:01,793 --> 00:11:04,212
if either of us
let work or practice slide.

215
00:11:04,879 --> 00:11:06,672
Since we knew
we had feelings for each other,

216
00:11:06,756 --> 00:11:08,925
we couldn't go back to how things were.

217
00:11:09,759 --> 00:11:12,970
I didn't wanna decide
based on a worst-case scenario,

218
00:11:13,054 --> 00:11:15,139
especially without giving it a shot.

219
00:11:16,724 --> 00:11:20,812
When you think about it, we're still
in the middle of a trial run, you know.

220
00:11:22,438 --> 00:11:23,439
Go for it!

221
00:11:24,023 --> 00:11:24,982
Keep it up!

222
00:11:25,066 --> 00:11:26,943
[Taiki] <i>I guess I had made the assumption</i>

223
00:11:27,026 --> 00:11:29,695
<i>that they were both
just good at everything.</i>

224
00:11:29,779 --> 00:11:30,696
EIMEI

225
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:31,948
WAKABAYASHI HIGH

226
00:11:33,783 --> 00:11:36,452
- That's it, you got this!
- [all cheering indistinctly]

227
00:11:40,081 --> 00:11:41,958
[referee] First game, winner...

228
00:11:42,041 --> 00:11:44,710
- Yes, Haryu. That's it.
- [all cheering]

229
00:11:44,794 --> 00:11:45,962
Nice one!

230
00:11:48,214 --> 00:11:52,885
[Taiki] <i>I have absolutely no idea
what Chinatsu is thinking.</i>

231
00:11:53,678 --> 00:11:57,140
<i>And I haven't told her
what's on my mind either.</i>

232
00:11:59,642 --> 00:12:02,270
[Hyodo] Good for you, Haryu.
Making it this far.

233
00:12:02,353 --> 00:12:04,981
Well, I have to hang in there
until our match.

234
00:12:05,606 --> 00:12:08,943
Too bad we'll see each other
in the third round instead of finals.

235
00:12:09,986 --> 00:12:11,279
Speaking of which,

236
00:12:11,362 --> 00:12:14,407
I hear that you had an interesting chat
with one of our first-years.

237
00:12:15,283 --> 00:12:18,161
About the two players
who will be here next year.

238
00:12:20,246 --> 00:12:22,915
If it were me and Taiki, would you be mad?

239
00:12:24,125 --> 00:12:26,169
The venue next year
will be different, though.

240
00:12:26,252 --> 00:12:27,920
[Haryu] Went right over his head.

241
00:12:28,004 --> 00:12:31,174
Nah, I wouldn't be mad at all
if it was the two of you.

242
00:12:31,257 --> 00:12:33,468
It's whoever wins prefecturals.

243
00:12:33,551 --> 00:12:34,427
Although,

244
00:12:35,052 --> 00:12:39,891
if you can't take me
in at least one game today, Haryu,

245
00:12:39,974 --> 00:12:41,684
you might not be here next year.

246
00:12:42,310 --> 00:12:44,312
What are you talking about?

247
00:12:44,395 --> 00:12:46,189
I came here to beat you today.

248
00:12:46,272 --> 00:12:47,940
[announcer on PA] <i>Your attention.</i>

249
00:12:48,024 --> 00:12:52,111
<i>Hyodo of Sajikawa High School,
and Haryu of Eimei High School,</i>

250
00:12:52,195 --> 00:12:54,697
<i>please make your way to court nine.</i>

251
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:56,199
[grunts]

252
00:12:56,282 --> 00:12:57,200
[inaudible]

253
00:12:58,784 --> 00:13:00,203
[tense music playing]

254
00:13:02,288 --> 00:13:03,331
[pants]

255
00:13:03,414 --> 00:13:05,791
[Hyodo] <i>That's what
I'm talking about, Haryu.</i>

256
00:13:06,792 --> 00:13:09,170
<i>If only you had been
more aggressive right of the bat,</i>

257
00:13:09,253 --> 00:13:10,671
<i>you could've scored a point.</i>

258
00:13:10,755 --> 00:13:13,216
<i>You're being too cautious
and too defensive.</i>

259
00:13:14,008 --> 00:13:17,094
<i>That's why you keep giving up
so many points.</i>

260
00:13:18,137 --> 00:13:20,598
<i>You can't shake the image of losing to me.</i>

261
00:13:21,307 --> 00:13:23,226
He already lost the first game.

262
00:13:23,309 --> 00:13:25,478
But he still has
a chance of winning, right?

263
00:13:25,561 --> 00:13:27,271
Yeah, we play to 21 points.

264
00:13:27,855 --> 00:13:29,315
Two games is a win.

265
00:13:30,191 --> 00:13:33,778
[Haryu] <i>Dammit,
I've fallen into Hyodo's rhythm.</i>

266
00:13:33,861 --> 00:13:36,113
<i>It's like a replay of prefecturals.</i>

267
00:13:37,281 --> 00:13:38,908
<i>She's looking pretty worried.</i>

268
00:13:40,826 --> 00:13:43,120
<i>It's rare to see her like that.</i>

269
00:13:43,204 --> 00:13:44,622
GRADE 5 CLASS 2 SCHEDULE

270
00:13:44,705 --> 00:13:47,708
[Haryu] <i>Karen and I first met
when we were in fifth grade.</i>

271
00:13:48,459 --> 00:13:51,629
{\an8}- Haryu!
- Can you help us with math after school?

272
00:13:51,712 --> 00:13:54,882
Sorry, I have swim lessons Wednesdays.

273
00:13:54,966 --> 00:13:57,718
[Haryu] <i>My parents encouraged me
to try a lot of things.</i>

274
00:13:58,302 --> 00:14:02,014
<i>Piano, Monday, swimming, Wednesday,
cram school, Saturday.</i>

275
00:14:02,098 --> 00:14:04,183
<i>Even calligraphy at one point.</i>

276
00:14:04,267 --> 00:14:05,810
<i>Somehow we found time,</i>

277
00:14:05,893 --> 00:14:08,521
<i>and my dad took me
to a badminton club one day,</i>

278
00:14:08,604 --> 00:14:10,648
<i>just for fun, and I really got into it.</i>

279
00:14:10,731 --> 00:14:12,400
<i>That's its own story though.</i>

280
00:14:12,483 --> 00:14:13,442
SWIMMING SCHOOL

281
00:14:13,526 --> 00:14:15,653
<i>I was pretty good at most things.</i>

282
00:14:15,736 --> 00:14:20,408
<i>I thought that in itself was my strength.
And then I met Karen.</i>

283
00:14:21,409 --> 00:14:25,413
We have a new friend joining us today.
This is Karen Moriya.

284
00:14:25,913 --> 00:14:27,373
It's very nice to meet you.

285
00:14:27,456 --> 00:14:29,125
- She's cute.
- She looks grown-up!

286
00:14:29,208 --> 00:14:31,002
She's pretty. Look how long her legs are!

287
00:14:31,085 --> 00:14:33,087
- [coach] Can you give us a swim?
- [Karen] Sure!

288
00:14:33,170 --> 00:14:34,338
[Haryu] <i>If you asked anyone,</i>

289
00:14:34,422 --> 00:14:37,675
<i>they'd say she was beautiful,
and that everyone would fall for...</i>

290
00:14:37,758 --> 00:14:39,886
<i>Well, you'd be wrong
about the second part.</i>

291
00:14:39,969 --> 00:14:43,055
[coach] Moriya! Use your legs!
No, those are your hands!

292
00:14:43,139 --> 00:14:45,182
[bubbling, gasping]

293
00:14:46,434 --> 00:14:48,144
- Yum, oxygen!
- [Haryu] Hey.

294
00:14:48,227 --> 00:14:49,061
Huh?

295
00:14:49,145 --> 00:14:52,148
Why'd you bother coming to a school
known for its swimming program?

296
00:14:52,231 --> 00:14:53,065
What?

297
00:14:53,149 --> 00:14:55,318
Doing something
that you're not any good at

298
00:14:55,943 --> 00:14:58,905
is just gonna set you up
to completely embarrass yourself.

299
00:14:59,655 --> 00:15:00,573
[groans softly]

300
00:15:01,365 --> 00:15:02,575
[Haryu gasps]

301
00:15:04,911 --> 00:15:06,329
[gasps] What are you doing?

302
00:15:06,412 --> 00:15:08,331
- So then you teach me!
- [exclaims]

303
00:15:09,248 --> 00:15:11,459
You feel bad I looked dumb
in front of everyone.

304
00:15:11,542 --> 00:15:13,628
So why don't you show me a thing or two?

305
00:15:13,711 --> 00:15:15,838
I came to this school to learn after all.

306
00:15:15,922 --> 00:15:18,090
Uh... I didn't mean it like that.

307
00:15:18,174 --> 00:15:20,718
[Karen] I can't stand
not being able to swim.

308
00:15:20,801 --> 00:15:23,429
'Cause my dream
is to swim with the dolphins.

309
00:15:23,512 --> 00:15:25,097
[Haryu] That's why you're here?

310
00:15:25,181 --> 00:15:28,809
[Karen] Yeah, and it's not fair to decide
that I'm bad at something

311
00:15:28,893 --> 00:15:31,604
without giving myself
a fair shot to learn.

312
00:15:32,605 --> 00:15:34,899
Just because I'm struggling right now,

313
00:15:34,982 --> 00:15:37,860
doesn't mean that I will
still be struggling with it in the future.

314
00:15:38,569 --> 00:15:39,779
[exclaims softly]

315
00:15:41,447 --> 00:15:43,783
[Haryu] <i>By the time she left our school,</i>

316
00:15:43,866 --> 00:15:46,994
<i>she was able to swim
the 50-meter freestyle.</i>

317
00:15:47,078 --> 00:15:48,704
<i>Even our coach was moved.</i>

318
00:15:50,247 --> 00:15:52,333
<i>After that, we went to different schools,</i>

319
00:15:52,416 --> 00:15:54,126
<i>but we lived close to each other.</i>

320
00:15:54,210 --> 00:15:56,629
<i>So we started to hang out together.</i>

321
00:15:56,712 --> 00:15:59,298
- 'Sup?
- What are you doing here?

322
00:15:59,382 --> 00:16:02,259
You said you won
your badminton tournament, so I thought...

323
00:16:02,343 --> 00:16:04,387
I'd let you have dinner with me.

324
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:08,391
{\an8}[Haryu] <i>We kept in touch about our lives,
and supported each other.</i>

325
00:16:08,474 --> 00:16:11,143
{\an8}<i>In spite of wanting
to take our relationship further,</i>

326
00:16:11,227 --> 00:16:14,689
<i>I kept making excuses,
thinking I shouldn't get in her way.</i>

327
00:16:17,233 --> 00:16:18,150
<i>That's why...</i>

328
00:16:18,234 --> 00:16:19,694
Oh, Kengo.

329
00:16:19,777 --> 00:16:21,153
I like you a lot.

330
00:16:22,363 --> 00:16:23,781
[Haryu] <i>...my heart ached.</i>

331
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:27,702
<i>Here was Karen,
the scent of shampoo lingering,</i>

332
00:16:27,785 --> 00:16:30,079
<i>her eyes looking shyly down.</i>

333
00:16:30,162 --> 00:16:32,790
<i>My heart ached, both,
from my feelings for her,</i>

334
00:16:32,873 --> 00:16:36,919
<i>and from the shame of not being the one
to confess my own feelings first.</i>

335
00:16:37,003 --> 00:16:38,421
[uplifting music playing]

336
00:16:39,005 --> 00:16:41,674
<i>She's always been the cool one.</i>

337
00:16:41,757 --> 00:16:43,551
<i>Just like she took on swimming,</i>

338
00:16:43,634 --> 00:16:45,636
<i>she always chose to challenge herself,</i>

339
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:48,931
<i>despite the fear and embarrassment
that might come along with it.</i>

340
00:16:49,515 --> 00:16:51,642
<i>That's the girlfriend watching me.</i>

341
00:16:51,726 --> 00:16:54,937
<i>If I don't find the cool side
of myself now, then when will I?</i>

342
00:16:56,605 --> 00:16:58,691
- [Taiki] He's catching up!
- [pants]

343
00:16:58,774 --> 00:16:59,942
You got this!

344
00:17:00,026 --> 00:17:01,444
[grunts]

345
00:17:01,527 --> 00:17:03,446
[Taiki] Haryu, keep it up!

346
00:17:03,529 --> 00:17:06,198
- Good footwork! Come on, take him down!
- [grunts]

347
00:17:07,283 --> 00:17:08,451
[all exclaiming]

348
00:17:11,287 --> 00:17:12,455
[pants]

349
00:17:12,538 --> 00:17:14,457
[Taiki] He's got a game on the board!

350
00:17:16,333 --> 00:17:18,502
[Haryu grunts] <i>I can win.</i>

351
00:17:18,586 --> 00:17:19,754
<i>There's still a chance.</i>

352
00:17:19,837 --> 00:17:20,755
[grunts]

353
00:17:20,838 --> 00:17:22,423
<i>I can't give up.</i>

354
00:17:22,506 --> 00:17:24,008
<i>My temperature's rising.</i>

355
00:17:24,091 --> 00:17:25,009
[grunts]

356
00:17:25,092 --> 00:17:26,761
<i>My feet are still with me.</i>

357
00:17:26,844 --> 00:17:29,805
- [Taiki] Go, Haryu!
- [Haryu] <i>I can hear them cheering me on.</i>

358
00:17:29,889 --> 00:17:31,265
<i>I'm still in good shape.</i>

359
00:17:31,891 --> 00:17:33,517
<i>My mind is calm.</i>

360
00:17:33,601 --> 00:17:34,769
[grunts]

361
00:17:35,519 --> 00:17:36,771
<i>Yet somehow,</i>

362
00:17:37,688 --> 00:17:40,274
<i>this three-point gap won't last forever.</i>

363
00:17:40,858 --> 00:17:42,485
<i>Narrow your focus.</i>

364
00:17:42,568 --> 00:17:44,028
<i>Watch your opponent.</i>

365
00:17:44,612 --> 00:17:47,907
<i>You won a game already.
Your abilities are just as strong as his.</i>

366
00:17:49,408 --> 00:17:51,410
<i>Keep your feet moving. React fast.</i>

367
00:17:51,494 --> 00:17:53,162
<i>Then you'll make it to the shuttle.</i>

368
00:17:53,996 --> 00:17:55,206
<i>You'll make it.</i>

369
00:17:56,248 --> 00:17:57,666
<i>You'll make it.</i>

370
00:17:58,417 --> 00:17:59,376
[music fades]

371
00:18:01,253 --> 00:18:02,296
[shuttlecock thuds]

372
00:18:02,379 --> 00:18:05,716
[referee] Match winner:
Hyodo of Sajikawa High School.

373
00:18:06,258 --> 00:18:08,177
[breathing shakily]

374
00:18:10,513 --> 00:18:12,431
- [all cheering]
- [Haryu] <i>Damn it.</i>

375
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:15,684
<i>I can't believe his smash
was still that powerful.</i>

376
00:18:15,768 --> 00:18:17,436
<i>I can't compete with that.</i>

377
00:18:18,354 --> 00:18:21,941
It's been fun going up against you...
these two years.

378
00:18:27,863 --> 00:18:30,699
[Haryu] Thank you... for everything.

379
00:18:30,783 --> 00:18:32,576
[moody music playing]

380
00:18:33,244 --> 00:18:36,914
Even from a player's perspective,
badminton matches end in a second.

381
00:18:36,997 --> 00:18:39,458
For real. They're over before you know it.

382
00:18:41,127 --> 00:18:42,711
I'm going on a quick run!

383
00:18:42,795 --> 00:18:44,713
Exercise after all that?

384
00:18:44,797 --> 00:18:47,216
That's what I said.
Watch this for me, would you?

385
00:18:48,425 --> 00:18:50,719
It's been said 1,000 times before,

386
00:18:50,803 --> 00:18:53,430
but seeing someone
work as hard as he does,

387
00:18:53,514 --> 00:18:55,224
makes you wanna do the same.

388
00:18:57,309 --> 00:18:58,811
[soft music playing]

389
00:19:01,313 --> 00:19:02,523
It really does.

390
00:19:03,149 --> 00:19:05,901
- I'm crossing my fingers for you, too.
- Thanks.

391
00:19:05,985 --> 00:19:07,695
For sports and romance!

392
00:19:07,778 --> 00:19:08,737
[exclaims]

393
00:19:09,321 --> 00:19:11,240
Will you tell her how you feel?

394
00:19:11,323 --> 00:19:14,743
You're already living together,
which is more than most couples get to do.

395
00:19:14,827 --> 00:19:17,663
It's <i>because</i> we live together
that I'm hesitant.

396
00:19:17,746 --> 00:19:19,790
- What?
- If she rejects me...

397
00:19:20,541 --> 00:19:23,752
I worry that she won't feel comfortable
at my house anymore.

398
00:19:24,253 --> 00:19:28,132
Living with us, Chinatsu is already
so polite and sensitive.

399
00:19:28,215 --> 00:19:32,178
Uh. Wait, but you have
a crush on Chii, right?

400
00:19:32,761 --> 00:19:33,637
Right.

401
00:19:33,721 --> 00:19:36,932
And, like, you want to be
in a relationship with her, right?

402
00:19:37,016 --> 00:19:38,893
Uh. [stutters] Yes.

403
00:19:38,976 --> 00:19:41,061
Then, isn't it a lot creepier

404
00:19:41,145 --> 00:19:44,148
if she's living with someone
who secretly has feelings for her?

405
00:19:44,231 --> 00:19:45,399
What?!

406
00:19:46,483 --> 00:19:48,277
[groans]

407
00:19:51,071 --> 00:19:53,574
<i>I hadn't thought of it like that.</i>

408
00:19:54,491 --> 00:19:55,492
<i>Karen's right.</i>

409
00:19:55,576 --> 00:19:57,703
<i>It might be creepy
if she has to live with a guy</i>

410
00:19:57,786 --> 00:19:59,538
{\an8}<i>who's constantly watching her,</i>

411
00:19:59,622 --> 00:20:02,166
<i>and sniffs the air
whenever she walks past.</i>

412
00:20:02,249 --> 00:20:03,417
[sighs]

413
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:05,377
C'mon, don't start overthinking it.

414
00:20:05,461 --> 00:20:09,673
Taiki, it can be nice to consider
how the other person might be feeling,

415
00:20:10,341 --> 00:20:15,429
but at the end of the day, you can't know
what Chii's actually thinking.

416
00:20:16,013 --> 00:20:17,473
Sometimes it's important

417
00:20:17,556 --> 00:20:20,184
that there are moments
you choose not to think too.

418
00:20:20,893 --> 00:20:22,186
The way things are going,

419
00:20:22,269 --> 00:20:25,606
you're gonna be rallying
against a wall your whole life.

420
00:20:25,689 --> 00:20:26,857
[grunts softly]

421
00:20:27,775 --> 00:20:29,360
Is that what you want?

422
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:33,572
[Taiki] No, I want a back-and-forth rally.

423
00:20:33,656 --> 00:20:35,282
[Karen] Okay. Then go for it.

424
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:39,370
[pants]

425
00:20:40,204 --> 00:20:41,330
[Karen] Welcome back.

426
00:20:41,956 --> 00:20:44,291
What? You're leaving?

427
00:20:44,375 --> 00:20:47,836
- Yeah, I've got a train to catch.
- Thanks so much for coming to this.

428
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:50,339
Oh, yeah, it was fun,
even beyond the match.

429
00:20:50,422 --> 00:20:51,507
[soft piano music playing]

430
00:20:52,174 --> 00:20:55,344
Kengo, this might be
a tough question to answer, but...

431
00:20:56,136 --> 00:20:59,890
For a second-year, is it hard
to get any better than you are right now?

432
00:20:59,974 --> 00:21:01,475
I mean, yeah, I'd say so.

433
00:21:02,351 --> 00:21:05,396
Almost everyone else
was a third-year, so there's that.

434
00:21:05,479 --> 00:21:06,981
- I gotcha.
- Hm?

435
00:21:07,648 --> 00:21:08,649
[sighs softly]

436
00:21:12,152 --> 00:21:13,737
Okay, then. I should get going.

437
00:21:16,573 --> 00:21:17,992
- Karen.
- [exclaims]

438
00:21:19,201 --> 00:21:22,496
Next time, I'll win more matches.

439
00:21:24,415 --> 00:21:25,374
Yeah.

440
00:21:28,252 --> 00:21:29,378
Ew, you're smelly.

441
00:21:29,461 --> 00:21:30,504
Uh, hey!

442
00:21:31,130 --> 00:21:33,924
All right. Go study up
on the other matches now.

443
00:21:34,008 --> 00:21:35,509
Yup. Get home safe.

444
00:21:35,592 --> 00:21:37,261
If what you said to me was a lie,

445
00:21:37,344 --> 00:21:39,388
I'm cutting down on our date nights.

446
00:21:39,471 --> 00:21:40,431
Yeah, I gotcha.

447
00:21:40,514 --> 00:21:43,392
<i>That's more of a punishment for you
than it is for me.</i>

448
00:21:51,358 --> 00:21:54,278
Hey, which court
is Hoshino High School playing on?

449
00:21:54,987 --> 00:21:56,280
It's court 11.

450
00:21:56,947 --> 00:21:58,157
Come with me, Taiki.

451
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,408
Yeah!

452
00:22:01,368 --> 00:22:03,912
[Taiki] <i>Wait. He smells good.</i>

453
00:22:04,997 --> 00:22:06,999
[closing theme song playing]
